      "size": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 320
      },
      "note": "## Play everywhere\n\nFixes files your TV or browser can't play as they are, so your media server doesn't have to convert them while you watch.\n\n- The video is re-encoded to **H.264** only when one of your devices can't play it.\n- When the default audio can't play there (DTS, TrueHD), a **stereo AAC** track is added and becomes the default. The original track stays.\n\nPick your devices on the **Shared values** card: both nodes follow **Devices**. Adding `chrome` covers browsers too, but browsers can't play HEVC everywhere, so HEVC files are then re-encoded to H.264 and get bigger."
